     "content": "### 1. The Revised Numbers\n\nHere is how the revised offer compares against your current compensation at Meta:\n\n| Component | Current Meta (IC6) | Revised Google (L6) | Delta |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $240,000 | Match |\n| **Target Bonus** | ~$36,000 (15%) | $48,000 (20%) | +$12,000/yr |\n| **Annualized Equity** | ~$250,000/yr | $320,000/yr *(avg)* | +$70,000/yr |\n| **4-Year Annualized Total Comp** | **~$526,000/yr** | **~$608,000/yr** | **+$82,000/yr (+15.6%)** |\n\n---\n\n### 2. The Impact of Google\u2019s Vesting Schedule (Year 1 & 2 Reality)\n\nGoogle standardly uses **front-loaded vesting** (typically **33% / 33% / 22% / 12%** over 4 years):\n\n* **Year 1:** $240k base + $48k bonus + **$422,400** equity (33%) = **~$710,400**\n* **Year 2:** $240k base + $48k bonus + **$422,400** equity (33%) = **~$710,400**\n* **Year 3:** $240k base + $48k bonus + **$281,600** equity (22%) + *refreshers* = **~$570,000+**\n* **Year 4:** $240k base + $48k bonus + **$153,600** equity (12%) + *refreshers* = **~$441,000+**\n\n#### Why they didn't give a sign-on bonus:\nInstead of paying a cash sign-on bonus, Google increased your equity grant by **+$200,000** ($1.08M $\\rightarrow$ $1.28M). Because Year 1 vests at ~33%, you are receiving roughly **~$140,000 more equity in Year 1 alone** than in their original offer, which effectively replaces the near-term unvested Meta stock you walked away from.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Should You Take It?\n\n**Yes, from a pure compensation perspective, this clears the threshold to accept.**\n\nHere is the breakdown by factor:\n\n#### Why Accept:\n1. **Strong Year 1\u20132 Comp:** Making **~$710,000/yr** in your first two years is a massive jump over your current ~$526,000 run-rate (a ~35% increase in gross earnings in Years 1 and 2).\n2. **Top-Tier Banding for L6:** A $1.28M equity grant at Google L6 is in the upper quartile (75th\u201385th percentile) for the role.\n3. **True Best & Final:** Google generally holds firm once equity is moved up by $200k and base is matched; pushing further without competing offers risks offer rescission or fatigue.\n\n#### When to Stay at Meta:\n* **Scope & Momentum:** If your current scope at Meta has clear visibility toward IC7 (Director/Principal level) in the next 12\u201318 months, leaving resets your internal political capital. Re-leveling to L7 at Google from L6 can take considerable time.\n* **Culture Preference:** If you thrive in Meta's fast-paced, high-execution environment and are hesitant about Google's consensus-driven product culture.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Summary Recommendation\n\nIf you are open to a new challenge and **compensation is your primary driver**, **accept the offer**. \n\nYou successfully pushed the total 4-year package from **$2.2M to $2.43M**, locked in top-band L6 equity, and guaranteed a significant income boost over the next 24 months.",
